# The versioned TER root-partition measurement artifacts are hash-verified byte
# streams: docs/root_partition_decision.md records SHA-256 digests of these exact
# files, and results/partition/task11-final-20260825/data-hashes.jsonl records a
# digest for every raw campaign file. core.autocrlf must therefore never rewrite
# their line endings, or the recorded digests stop verifying after a checkout.
/results/** -text
# The manuscript uses exact-byte SHA-256 manifests for its frozen inputs too.
# Preserve both LF and CRLF originals on every platform and checkout.
/paper/data/** -text
# These sources mix CRLF and LF line endings, and the three ARWLF campaign builds
# recorded their SHA-256 in that exact form (results/arwlf/*/source_manifest.txt).
# Storing them unconverted lets reviewer/check_build_sources.py recover them
# byte-exactly from any clone.
/bench/ter_q3report_bench.cpp -text
/bench/ter_q3report_crossover_bench.cpp -text
/bench/ter_q3report_paper_crossover_bench.cpp -text
/include/ter/q3report_audit.hpp -text
/include/ter/q3report_crossover.hpp -text
/include/ter/q3report_paper_crossover.hpp -text
/src/q3report_audit.cpp -text
/src/q3report_crossover.cpp -text
/src/q3report_paper_crossover.cpp -text
